insert into public.lessons (id, course_id, module_id, title, kind, content, video_url, duration_minutes, position, is_preview)
values ($dbi$957247a1-7c11-5df6-b688-3c70b19dc19e$dbi$, $dbi$8ae7861b-b5f1-5a64-afaa-3115e1a70e2b$dbi$, $dbi$587040d6-33fd-5edb-bf73-7fe184833aa1$dbi$, $dbi$Welcome to the grid$dbi$, $dbi$article$dbi$, $dbi$A **spreadsheet** is a grid made of **rows** (numbered 1, 2, 3…) and **columns** (lettered A, B, C…). Where a row and column meet is a **cell**, named by its column then row: **B3** is column B, row 3. A file is called a **workbook**, and each tab at the bottom is a **worksheet** (or sheet).

### Why spreadsheets matter
- **Automatic calculations** — change one number and every total updates.
- **Organisation** — thousands of rows of data in a neat table.
- **Analysis** — sort, filter, summarise and chart in seconds.
- **Everywhere** — Excel, Google Sheets and LibreOffice Calc all work the same way.

### Finding your way around
- The **Name Box** (top-left) shows the selected cell's address.
- The **Formula Bar** shows what is really inside the cell — a number, text or formula.
- A **range** is a block of cells written with a colon: `A1:C10` means from A1 down to C10.
- `Ctrl + Arrow key` jumps to the edge of your data; `Ctrl + Home` returns to A1.

### Types of data
| Type | Example | Tip |
|---|---|---|
| Text | `Kumasi`, `Product name` | Left-aligned by default |
| Number | `250`, `12.5` | Right-aligned by default — never type "GH₵" inside the number |
| Date | `15/03/2026` | Stored as a number, so you can calculate with it |
| Formula | `=B2*C2` | Always starts with `=` |

> [!TIP]
> If a number is left-aligned, the spreadsheet may be treating it as text. That often happens when you copy data from the web or type a space before it.

> [!TRY]
> Open a new spreadsheet. In A1 type **Item**, in B1 **Quantity**, in C1 **Price (GH₵)**. Add five items you might buy at the market with quantities and prices.$dbi$, null, 8, 1, true)
on conflict (id) do update set module_id = excluded.module_id, title = excluded.title, kind = excluded.kind, content = excluded.content, video_url = excluded.video_url, duration_minutes = excluded.duration_minutes, position = excluded.position, is_preview = excluded.is_preview;
