values ($dbi$8e1c0764-57d1-5737-ab38-0c91e0cb570f$dbi$, $dbi$web-development-foundations$dbi$, $dbi$Web Development Foundations: HTML & CSS$dbi$, $dbi$Build and publish your own responsive website from scratch — no experience needed.$dbi$, $dbi$Every website you visit — from news sites to online shops — is built with three languages: HTML for structure, CSS for style and JavaScript for interaction. This course teaches the first two in depth, so you can build beautiful, responsive pages yourself.

You will write real code from the very first lesson, and finish by publishing your own portfolio website on the internet. Web development is one of the most in-demand digital skills in Ghana and around the world, and it can lead to freelance work, internships and a career in tech.$dbi$, (select id from public.categories where slug = $dbi$software-development$dbi$), $dbi$beginner$dbi$, 'English', null, 'published', array[$dbi$Explain how websites work and what HTML, CSS and JavaScript each do$dbi$, $dbi$Structure web pages with semantic HTML — headings, lists, links, images and forms$dbi$, $dbi$Style pages with CSS colours, fonts, spacing and the box model$dbi$, $dbi$Build modern layouts with Flexbox and CSS Grid$dbi$, $dbi$Make websites responsive so they look great on phones$dbi$, $dbi$Publish a personal portfolio website online for free$dbi$]::text[], array[$dbi$Basic computer skills (see Digital Literacy Essentials)$dbi$, $dbi$A computer with a browser. A free code editor such as VS Code is recommended, but you can practise in an online editor like CodePen$dbi$]::text[], array[$dbi$html$dbi$, $dbi$css$dbi$, $dbi$web design$dbi$, $dbi$responsive$dbi$, $dbi$flexbox$dbi$, $dbi$portfolio$dbi$]::text[], 70, 10, true, true, false, now())
