values ($dbi$3c8e66b9-e5e7-538e-b881-2842cdd65aba$dbi$, $dbi$8e1c0764-57d1-5737-ab38-0c91e0cb570f$dbi$, $dbi$ed73ba43-a926-5aa7-a3bb-f528456aa7cc$dbi$, $dbi$Tables for data$dbi$, $dbi$article$dbi$, $dbi$Use HTML tables for **tabular data** — timetables, price lists, results — not for page layout.

```html
<table>
  <caption>SHS 2 Science Timetable</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Day</th>
      <th>Subject</th>
      <th>Time</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Monday</td>
      <td>Physics</td>
      <td>8:00 – 9:30</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Tuesday</td>
      <td>Chemistry</td>
      <td>10:00 – 11:30</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>
```

### The table tags
- `<table>` wraps the whole table.
- `<caption>` gives it a title (good for accessibility).
- `<thead>` and `<tbody>` group the header and body rows.
- `<tr>` is a **table row**.
- `<th>` is a **header cell** (bold and centred by default).
- `<td>` is a **data cell**.

### Spanning cells
- `colspan="2"` makes a cell stretch across two columns.
- `rowspan="2"` makes a cell stretch down two rows.

```html
<td colspan="3">Break</td>
```

> [!TIP]
> Tables can overflow on small phone screens. Wrap them in a `<div style="overflow-x:auto">` so users can scroll sideways.

> [!TRY]
> Build a table of your weekly timetable or a price list for a small shop, with a caption, a header row and at least five rows.$dbi$, null, 8, 2, false)
